WEBVTT

00:00:00.330 --> 00:00:04.010
Please, magical violin, sing for me!

00:00:04.010 --> 00:00:05.930
More, more!

00:01:48.630 --> 00:01:52.130
Partita of Grief

00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:27.030
Hino-san!

00:02:39.740 --> 00:02:40.630
Hino...

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:43.930
Kaho-sempai...

00:02:48.170 --> 00:02:54.080
The seventh performer will be from Year 3, Class B in the Music Department, Azuma Yunoki-kun.

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:59.380
He will be performing Partita for Solo Flute, by Bach.

00:03:00.740 --> 00:03:04.090
It suits you perfectly, Yunoki-sama!

00:03:04.090 --> 00:03:06.040
Every time I see him it's so inspiring!

00:03:06.340 --> 00:03:09.460
I wonder if Kaho-sempai is OK?

00:03:09.460 --> 00:03:11.570
Maybe we should go check on her.

00:03:11.570 --> 00:03:13.460
Yeah, that's true.

00:03:14.180 --> 00:03:15.480
Just leave her be.

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:16.050
But...

00:03:17.310 --> 00:03:19.760
Just leave her alone till she calms down.

00:03:32.130 --> 00:03:34.880
Man, everything's all messed up.

00:03:44.600 --> 00:03:47.930
Everyone is upset thanks to Hino.

00:03:48.880 --> 00:03:52.330
Hihara, Tsuchiura, and even Tsukimori.

00:03:53.050 --> 00:03:55.070
Everyone's focused on her.

00:03:57.920 --> 00:04:01.600
But I won't be disturbed by anything.

00:04:04.450 --> 00:04:06.390
I'm going to try to give it my all.

00:04:09.570 --> 00:04:12.560
I'm not going to give up halfway!

00:04:17.720 --> 00:04:20.570
Isn't it difficult for you, Sempai?

00:04:47.350 --> 00:04:50.090
This is a different Yunoki-kun than we've heard before.

00:04:50.090 --> 00:04:52.650
He's being serious this time.

00:05:06.840 --> 00:05:08.200
Yunoki-sama!

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:09.280
It was wonderful!

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:11.540
What a wonderful performance!

00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:12.930
I'm moved!

00:05:12.930 --> 00:05:15.080
You'll get the grand prize, no doubt about it!

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:31.330
We will now announce the results for Seiso Academy's School-wide Competition third selection.

00:05:33.580 --> 00:05:36.560
7th place: Hino Kahoka-san.

00:05:37.580 --> 00:05:40.260
Is Kaho-chan OK?

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:44.570
6th place: Kazuki Hihara-kun.

00:05:45.900 --> 00:05:49.080
5th place: Keiichi Shimizu-kun.

00:05:50.380 --> 00:05:53.600
4th place: Shoko Fuyuumi-san.

00:05:57.500 --> 00:06:01.200
3rd place: Ryotaro Tsuchiura-kun.

00:06:04.090 --> 00:06:07.260
2nd place: Len Tsukimori-kun.

00:06:08.550 --> 00:06:11.170
So Tsukimori-kun was second place?

00:06:11.170 --> 00:06:12.010
Yeah.

00:06:12.780 --> 00:06:14.520
So that means first place is...

00:06:15.330 --> 00:06:17.100
Azuma Yunoki-kun!

00:06:18.270 --> 00:06:19.700
Yunoki-sama!

00:06:19.700 --> 00:06:21.330
Congratulations!

00:06:21.330 --> 00:06:23.240
Yunoki-sama!

00:06:23.900 --> 00:06:25.860
Yunoki-sama!

00:06:30.750 --> 00:06:35.530
Now, if you please, one more round of applause for the participants in the third selection.

00:06:37.620 --> 00:06:39.270
Kahoko Hino.

00:06:40.100 --> 00:06:41.730
Are you OK?

00:06:41.730 --> 00:06:42.660
Lili.

00:06:43.210 --> 00:06:45.490
What in the world happened?

00:06:45.490 --> 00:06:47.860
Three strings broke!

00:06:47.860 --> 00:06:50.220
And I saw it!

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:53.350
When the strings broke, there was this red light!

00:06:53.560 --> 00:06:56.520
Hey, what happened to this violin?

00:06:58.350 --> 00:07:02.270
That violin is a mirror that reflects your heart.

00:07:03.740 --> 00:07:10.560
If you love music, and have fun performing from your heart, that violin will play freely.

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:17.030
But if you rush hastily to improve yourself, the tone will waver.

00:07:17.030 --> 00:07:21.270
And the magic may have been depleted more rapidly than I thought.

00:07:21.270 --> 00:07:25.220
The violin wasn't able to react to your heart.

00:07:28.250 --> 00:07:30.770
My heart?

00:07:32.240 --> 00:07:37.100
Let me play more beautifully, more accurately, ring higher!

00:07:37.810 --> 00:07:42.000
Sing for me, more, more, more!

00:07:43.380 --> 00:07:45.190
It's my fault.

00:07:45.760 --> 00:07:48.280
I'm sorry! I'm so sorry!

00:07:48.280 --> 00:07:51.210
It's my fault that this happened.

00:07:51.700 --> 00:07:52.990
I'm sorry!

00:07:54.490 --> 00:07:56.950
You don't have to blame yourself.

00:07:56.950 --> 00:08:02.370
And I can fix the violin right away, so worry not!

00:08:02.370 --> 00:08:03.420
There!

00:08:11.140 --> 00:08:12.090
Lili?

00:08:12.090 --> 00:08:15.390
What? Why didn't that fix it?

00:08:15.390 --> 00:08:16.510
One more time!

00:08:21.110 --> 00:08:24.150
Why? That should have worked!

00:08:31.890 --> 00:08:34.160
That's enough...

00:08:34.370 --> 00:08:35.490
What?

00:08:35.830 --> 00:08:37.710
That's enough already.

00:08:37.710 --> 00:08:42.710
Even if you fix it, once I play it'll just happen again!

00:08:43.190 --> 00:08:45.170
Kahoko Hino...

00:08:45.440 --> 00:08:47.960
Look at what I've done to it...

00:08:47.960 --> 00:08:49.170
I...

00:08:50.210 --> 00:08:53.830
I have no right to love the violin!

00:08:55.890 --> 00:08:57.350
Good work today, everyone.

00:08:57.640 --> 00:09:01.710
Yunoki-kun, your performance today was really excellent.

00:09:01.710 --> 00:09:03.370
Thank you very much.

00:09:04.730 --> 00:09:05.840
Um...

00:09:05.840 --> 00:09:07.480
Where is Kaho-chan?

00:09:08.720 --> 00:09:09.990
Kanayan...

00:09:16.330 --> 00:09:17.620
Hino-san?

00:09:18.060 --> 00:09:18.870
Kaho?

00:09:25.870 --> 00:09:27.420
Hino-san!

00:09:27.420 --> 00:09:28.820
Kaho-sempai?

00:09:28.820 --> 00:09:30.060
Kaho-chan!

00:09:36.170 --> 00:09:37.650
Hino-san.

00:09:37.650 --> 00:09:38.860
Kaho-chan.

00:09:38.860 --> 00:09:39.990
Are you OK?

00:09:40.400 --> 00:09:43.700
Yeah. I'm sorry for worrying you.

00:09:46.990 --> 00:09:50.960
Thanks, everyone. I'm going to go home for today.

00:09:55.690 --> 00:09:59.020
Yunoki-sama, excellent effort today.

00:09:59.020 --> 00:10:02.950
Your performances are always amazing, but today was something special.

00:10:03.230 --> 00:10:06.670
I'm already looking forward to the final selection.

00:10:06.670 --> 00:10:07.750
Thank you.

00:10:08.360 --> 00:10:10.000
Yunoki-sama!

00:10:11.860 --> 00:10:13.000
If I may...

00:10:22.900 --> 00:10:25.150
Will you stop for a moment?

00:10:32.690 --> 00:10:37.360
From my perspective, for me to forget myself during the performance like that...

00:10:38.010 --> 00:10:41.380
And I thought I'd been perfect up until now.

00:10:43.220 --> 00:10:47.610
OK, that's enough. That was some very good playing there.

00:10:47.610 --> 00:10:51.230
You are improving faster than any of your brothers.

00:10:51.230 --> 00:10:55.130
Pretty soon you'll have caught up to your older brothers.

00:10:55.130 --> 00:10:56.960
Thank you very much.

00:10:57.280 --> 00:11:00.800
Azuma-san. You will quit the piano.

00:11:00.800 --> 00:11:02.160
Grandmother.

00:11:02.160 --> 00:11:05.670
Your brothers already play the piano.

00:11:05.670 --> 00:11:07.750
Why don't you play a different instrument?

00:11:07.750 --> 00:11:08.820
But...

00:11:09.980 --> 00:11:12.320
I won't allow you to talk back to me.

00:11:15.760 --> 00:11:17.490
I have returned home.

00:11:18.130 --> 00:11:21.490
Aren't you quite a bit late?

00:11:21.490 --> 00:11:24.330
I apologize, Grandmother.

00:11:24.330 --> 00:11:29.790
I heard that you were accepted into Seiso Academy's Music Department.

00:11:29.790 --> 00:11:33.500
Does this mean you wish to continue on with music in college?

00:11:33.720 --> 00:11:37.030
No, I haven't completely made up my mind yet.

00:11:37.030 --> 00:11:41.570
I am also considering economics, commerce, or perhaps law.

00:11:41.570 --> 00:11:46.220
You are known as the third son. A member of the flower arranging house of Yunoki.

00:11:46.220 --> 00:11:50.370
Indeed, you must acquiring a deep knowledge of the arts,

00:11:50.370 --> 00:11:54.980
but eventually your duty will be to assist your father and brothers.

00:11:55.190 --> 00:11:58.190
You understand this, Azuma-san?

00:12:00.820 --> 00:12:01.760
Yes.

00:12:04.450 --> 00:12:07.910
I know, Grandmother.

00:12:08.870 --> 00:12:13.630
The younger brother cannot be allowed to surpass his older siblings.

00:12:13.630 --> 00:12:15.900
In other words, I am below them.

00:12:15.900 --> 00:12:18.830
No matter what happens, that's the implicit rule.

00:12:19.450 --> 00:12:22.050
I play well while keeping control.

00:12:22.050 --> 00:12:27.010
The flute that my Grandfather recommended I play was only supposed to be a hobby.

00:12:27.010 --> 00:12:31.250
And there were no arts in Seiso Academy's General Studies.

00:12:31.730 --> 00:12:35.690
And my future would be to support Yunoki's business.

00:12:37.370 --> 00:12:39.600
What a boring life that would be.

00:12:44.510 --> 00:12:50.160
Sheesh, ever since I met her, everything has gone awry.

00:12:50.900 --> 00:12:53.350
Kahoko Hino.

00:13:10.020 --> 00:13:12.620
Studying abroad?

00:13:13.100 --> 00:13:17.460
I have been thinking you should attend college in England.

00:13:17.460 --> 00:13:20.320
Since you are aiming to support the Yunoki business in the future,

00:13:20.540 --> 00:13:23.780
I believe it would be best for you to get some international experience.

00:13:24.020 --> 00:13:29.240
Before you enter college, transfer to a high school over there and acclimate yourself.

00:13:29.240 --> 00:13:33.830
I've made all the necessary preparations for you to go before the new term starts there.

00:13:33.830 --> 00:13:37.920
There are many things to take care of, so you will be leaving soon.

00:13:37.920 --> 00:13:40.320
But, the competition is not over yet.

00:13:40.320 --> 00:13:45.760
Music should only have been a hobby of yours, right, Azuma-san?

00:13:50.420 --> 00:13:52.780
Kaho-chan still hasn't come...

00:13:52.780 --> 00:13:54.020
Yeah...

00:13:54.290 --> 00:13:56.620
Is she really OK, I wonder?

00:13:59.470 --> 00:14:00.770
Good morning!

00:14:01.220 --> 00:14:03.060
That was close!

00:14:03.060 --> 00:14:04.860
I kinda overslept a little!

00:14:05.080 --> 00:14:07.450
G-Good morning...

00:14:13.540 --> 00:14:16.000
Oh, you've already been to that shop in front of the train station?

00:14:16.270 --> 00:14:17.320
Yeah.

00:14:17.320 --> 00:14:18.760
How was it?

00:14:18.760 --> 00:14:21.090
They had a bunch of different types of cakes, and they were pretty good.

00:14:21.330 --> 00:14:23.680
I wish I could have gone...

00:14:27.690 --> 00:14:30.340
Hey, wanna hang out somewhere on the way home?

00:14:31.430 --> 00:14:34.450
But, is that OK, Kaho?

00:14:35.290 --> 00:14:36.490
Is what OK?

00:14:37.200 --> 00:14:39.460
Like, what about practice?

00:14:39.460 --> 00:14:41.410
You were here during lunch, too.

00:14:41.410 --> 00:14:45.290
What's with you? You don't want to hang out with me or something?

00:14:45.290 --> 00:14:46.390
No!

00:14:46.390 --> 00:14:48.250
We're glad! But...

00:14:48.250 --> 00:14:50.120
Then it's decided.

00:14:50.120 --> 00:14:54.090
Now hurry up. Let's go to that shop in from of the train station.

00:14:54.090 --> 00:14:55.110
Sure.

00:14:55.110 --> 00:14:57.500
Wait, let me get ready.

00:15:00.780 --> 00:15:04.760
That's right. Hanging out with friends on the way home from school.

00:15:06.250 --> 00:15:08.370
Talking about silly little things...

00:15:10.870 --> 00:15:12.290
Laughing...

00:15:15.350 --> 00:15:18.420
It's just like it was back before the competition.

00:15:20.560 --> 00:15:22.540
Before the competition...

00:15:23.500 --> 00:15:24.790
I'm home!

00:15:38.810 --> 00:15:41.580
I have no right to play the violin.

00:15:42.640 --> 00:15:45.430
I have no right to say I love the violin.

00:15:55.720 --> 00:15:59.750
Did something happen to Kaho-chan during the third selection performance?

00:15:59.750 --> 00:16:01.570
I heard about it from Kanayan afterwards.

00:16:02.370 --> 00:16:05.900
I was just so focused on myself the whole time...

00:16:07.480 --> 00:16:10.780
Even though Kaho-chan was hurting so badly.

00:16:12.380 --> 00:16:13.560
And yet, I...

00:16:14.180 --> 00:16:15.870
I'm a horrible person.

00:16:19.220 --> 00:16:20.500
Thanks for waiting!

00:16:27.160 --> 00:16:30.240
She went home again today?

00:16:30.240 --> 00:16:34.230
Even though she was working perhaps even too hard up until now.

00:16:34.230 --> 00:16:36.350
Did her nerve finally snap?

00:16:39.150 --> 00:16:42.400
Oh, welcome home, Len.

00:16:42.400 --> 00:16:46.110
I just poured some tea. Would you like some?

00:16:47.410 --> 00:16:48.440
Yes.

00:16:50.990 --> 00:16:52.280
Thank you.

00:16:53.670 --> 00:16:57.530
I'm going to perform at a charity concert next.

00:16:57.790 --> 00:16:58.730
Yes.

00:16:58.730 --> 00:17:03.000
And the sponsor asked me if you would also like to perform?

00:17:04.200 --> 00:17:06.970
He said he'd like it if we performed together.

00:17:07.420 --> 00:17:09.710
Together? Us?

00:17:11.070 --> 00:17:15.510
Just one piece. I think it sounds like a good idea, what about you?

00:17:18.540 --> 00:17:20.110
I'm sorry.

00:17:23.680 --> 00:17:25.350
There's still time.

00:17:25.690 --> 00:17:30.360
I realize you are busy with the competition right now, but please consider it, Len.

00:17:31.820 --> 00:17:35.500
I am not yet at that level.

00:17:39.180 --> 00:17:41.870
If that boy would just find love somewhere...

00:17:54.500 --> 00:17:56.380
Hey, Kahoko!

00:17:56.380 --> 00:17:59.740
We're all planning to go to karaoke after this. Wanna come?

00:17:59.740 --> 00:18:00.970
I'll come, I'll come!

00:18:04.260 --> 00:18:07.190
Sorry, she has a previous engagement.

00:18:07.500 --> 00:18:10.180
Hey, Tsuchiura-kun, wait!

00:18:10.180 --> 00:18:11.320
Just wait a second!

00:18:11.510 --> 00:18:13.440
OK, Tsuchiura-kun?

00:18:13.440 --> 00:18:14.570
Let me go!

00:18:21.600 --> 00:18:23.370
What's with you all of a sudden?

00:18:23.580 --> 00:18:26.000
You haven't played at all lately, have you?

00:18:29.190 --> 00:18:32.800
What are you doing? The next selection is coming soon!

00:18:33.010 --> 00:18:35.300
Didn't you practice so much already?

00:18:35.890 --> 00:18:40.840
It was an accident. Just reset your feelings and recover next time.

00:18:40.840 --> 00:18:46.020
You know how much it takes to come back after missing just one day of practice, right?

00:18:46.720 --> 00:18:50.480
It was a mistake for me to enter the competition after all.

00:18:51.510 --> 00:18:54.050
What are you saying? Now's not the...

00:18:54.050 --> 00:18:57.150
So, just leave me alone.

00:18:57.150 --> 00:19:00.750
What's that supposed to mean? You're not acting like yourself.

00:19:01.570 --> 00:19:03.660
Enough, I quit!

00:19:06.540 --> 00:19:07.800
I withdraw.

00:19:08.780 --> 00:19:10.650
What are you saying?

00:19:10.650 --> 00:19:14.090
I don't want to anymore. That's what I've decided.

00:19:14.320 --> 00:19:16.300
I'll tell Kanazawa-sensei.

00:19:17.410 --> 00:19:19.940
Hey, what's the meaning of this?

00:19:19.940 --> 00:19:20.970
Hey, Hino!

00:19:22.930 --> 00:19:26.450
You have nothing to do with it, Tsuchiura-kun!

00:19:27.310 --> 00:19:29.480
Yes I do!

00:19:29.690 --> 00:19:31.780
It's because you were there that I...

00:19:39.500 --> 00:19:40.660
Dammit...

00:19:42.810 --> 00:19:45.250
I'm going home.

00:19:49.510 --> 00:19:53.330
Hino, are you running away?! Don't give me that crap!

00:19:55.710 --> 00:19:59.000
I'm different than Tsuchiura-kun.

00:20:05.980 --> 00:20:06.890
What the hell?!

00:20:12.340 --> 00:20:16.270
It's got to be him, let's call him.

00:20:16.570 --> 00:20:18.650
I'll go looking for him.

00:20:19.400 --> 00:20:22.360
Until the competition is over he's on leave.

00:20:22.570 --> 00:20:24.050
I know that, but...

00:20:27.160 --> 00:20:28.960
Hey, Tsuchiura!

00:20:30.140 --> 00:20:33.710
Perfect timing! I was just about to go looking for you!

00:20:36.500 --> 00:20:38.900
What's the matter, Sasaki?

00:20:38.900 --> 00:20:43.010
Iwazaki hurt his leg and is out of the regulars for a while.

00:20:43.710 --> 00:20:46.050
The district tournament's already started, hasn't it?

00:20:46.280 --> 00:20:50.090
Yeah. So, please come back, Tsuchiura!

00:20:50.090 --> 00:20:51.600
You're the only one we can count on!

00:20:55.330 --> 00:20:58.070
You'll come back, right?

00:21:01.780 --> 00:21:03.390
Tsuchiura!

00:21:04.440 --> 00:21:07.580
Tsuchiura, you don't have to bother.

00:21:07.580 --> 00:21:09.540
This isn't your problem.

00:21:11.070 --> 00:21:14.700
Tsuchiura, what is the only thing for you?

00:21:15.750 --> 00:21:19.540
If you are going to return to the soccer team, withdraw from the competition.

00:21:19.540 --> 00:21:22.800
And if you want to continue playing the piano, quit the soccer team.

00:21:23.260 --> 00:21:24.720
Captain, what are you saying?

00:21:25.820 --> 00:21:29.430
I have no need for people who can't decide and do everything halfway.

00:21:36.090 --> 00:21:39.310
Do I only do things halfway?

00:21:39.840 --> 00:21:43.400
Do I have any right to criticize Hino?

00:21:54.290 --> 00:21:57.260
I have no right to play the violin.

00:23:36.220 --> 00:23:39.730
Lili's One Point Classic!

00:23:39.980 --> 00:23:46.780
The great 18th century German composer, Bach, left us with over 1000 works in all genres except for opera.

00:23:46.780 --> 00:23:55.020
There were over 50 people in the Bach family, but the most famous was Johann Sebastian Bach, or "The Great Bach,"

00:23:55.020 --> 00:23:57.740
as well as "The Father of Music."

00:23:57.740 --> 00:23:59.730
OK, now time for a quiz!

00:23:59.730 --> 00:24:04.750
Bach is famous for his numerous children, so how many kids did he actually have?

00:24:05.770 --> 00:24:08.240
I wonder if Kaho-sempai is OK?

00:24:08.240 --> 00:24:12.310
I'm worried... In the meantime, maybe we could handle the preview in her place?

00:24:12.310 --> 00:24:13.990
I-Is that OK?

00:24:13.990 --> 00:24:16.760
Next episode: Pavane for a Lost Heart.

00:24:17.070 --> 00:24:20.060
But I thought I was gonna say it!

00:24:20.670 --> 00:24:24.200
The answer is... 20 children!
